# Paths excluded from the TruffleHog full-history scan.
#
# One Go-style regex per line, matched against the repository-relative path.
# Keep this list minimal and justify every entry: a path listed here stops
# being scanned across the whole of history, for every detector.
#
# Do not quote an excluded credential literally in this file. The scanner
# reads this file too, so a documented example becomes a new finding.
#
# internal/registry/sync_test.go
#   TestSyncURLPolicyRejectsCredentialsMalformedAuthoritiesAndDowngrades
#   asserts that credential-bearing URLs are REJECTED, so the corpus
#   necessarily contains one: an https URL carrying the literal words "user"
#   and "password" as userinfo, pointing at example.test -- a domain reserved
#   and unroutable per RFC 6761. There is no secret and nothing to rotate.
#
#   The current source splits that string so the literal never appears
#   contiguously; commit fa366dcabb830af4 still holds the un-split form. That
#   is why diff-scoped pull_request scans pass while full-history scans
#   (schedule, workflow_dispatch) flag it.
#
#   Verified with TruffleHog 3.97.4: verified_secrets 0, unverified_secrets 1,
#   detector URI. With this exclusion the same scan reports 0 while still
#   covering ~8.6k chunks, and a planted URI in another file is still caught.
^internal/registry/sync_test\.go$
